  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed first-floor rear extension and single-storey rear extension, by reason of their excessive depth, scale and siting, would result in an overbearing form of development causing an unacceptable sense of enclosure and loss of light to the occupiers of Nos. 190 and 194 Great West Road. The proposal would therefore harm neighbouring residential amenity, contrary to Policy SC7 of the Hounslow Local Plan and the Residential Extension Guidelines.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal, by virtue of its excessive scale, width, depth, bulk and design, would fail to appear subordinate to the host dwelling. The development would significantly alter the established roof form of the semi-detached pair, create a dominant and box-like appearance, and result in an incongruous form of development that would be harmful to the character and appearance of the host dwelling, the semi-detached pair and the surrounding area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Local Plan Policies SC7, CC1 and CC2, and the Residential Extension Guidelines."
  ],
